interim tabGroups/debugger sections, and popup sizing/scrolling) — TEMPORARY, never commit the applied result.

Apply:   git apply .claude/task132.4-harness.patch      (touches Detour/App/AppDelegate.swift only, #if DEBUG)
Build:   xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug -derivedDataPath .derived build
Run:     .claude/scratch/task132.4/drive-popup.sh <data dir name> <out dir> [front|activate]
         starts fixture_server.py on 127.0.0.1:18324, creates the isolated profile, seeds TestExtensions/api-explorer
         and the three popup fixtures in .claude/scratch/task132.4/popup-fixtures (fits, nowidth, grow) with seed.py,
         launches with DETOUR_DNR_HARNESS_DIR / DETOUR_DNR_HARNESS_URL and waits for DONE in harness.log.
         DETOUR_DNR_HARNESS_SIZING=0 skips the fixtures, DETOUR_DNR_HARNESS_EXPLORER=0 skips the API Explorer part.
Modes:   (none)    the app stays in the background; clicks are real NSEvents handed to the popup web view's
                   mouseDown/mouseUp (an inactive app's event queue does not deliver posted mouse events).
         front     also orders the window front regardless (bottom-right corner; no activation, not key) —
                   needed for WebKit to run rendering updates (resize observers, wheel scrolling).
         activate  activates the app for the run and re-activates the previous app afterwards (not needed so far).
What:    opens each popup with ExtensionPopoverController.show (the sidebar / Extensions-menu path), scrolls with
         wheel events, clicks buttons, logs what the popup shows and the popup's size / scrollability, and writes a
         WKWebView.takeSnapshot PNG per step. The URL text field of the API Explorer section is filled by script.
Review:  also runs the TASK-150 review scenarios (DETOUR_DNR_HARNESS_REVIEW=0 skips them): a popup whose document
         is taller than its body (popup-fixtures/tallish), and re-clicking the toolbar button while a popup is open
         (through BrowserWindowController.tabSidebarDidRequestShowExtensionPopup, the path a click takes).
         Popovers are closed without animation: with the screen locked an animated close never completes.
